crocirculation damage and may experience conditions like hypoalbuminemia due to dilution. As a result, they necessitate careful evaluation of their nutritional status and may require parenteral nutrition to support their health. Overall, \"PACIENTES CRÍTICOS\" are characterized by their need for close monitoring and tailored medical attention to address their compromised health.", "FÁRMACOS VASOPRESORES:Los fármacos vasopresores son medicamentos utilizados para aumentar la presión arterial en pacientes hipotensos, y su uso debe ser monitoreado durante la nutrición enteral.", "ATROFIA DE LA MUCOSA GÁSTRICA:La atrofia de la mucosa gástrica es una condición que puede prevenirse mediante la administración adecuada de nutrición enteral en pacientes críticos.", "SIGNOS DE ISQUEMIA:Los signos de isquemia incluyen distensión abdominal, cantidad de residuo gástrico y presencia de acidosis metabólica, que deben ser vigilados en pacientes que reciben nutrición enteral.", "MICROCIRCULACIÓN INTESTINAL:", "SEPSIS SEVERA:SEPSIS SEVERA is a severe condition characterized by a life-threatening response to infection, which leads to injury of the body's own tissues and organs. This condition was included as part of the study criteria for patients who were receiving various nutritional support methods. The severity of sepsis underscores its critical nature in clinical settings, highlighting the importance of effective management and intervention strategies.", "FÓRMULA DE NE:Formula de NE refers to the specific nutritional formulas used in enteral nutrition for patients, tailored to their medical needs.", "CANADIAN GUIDELINES:The Canadian guidelines provide recommendations for nutritional support in critically ill patients, particularly regarding the use of specific formulas and supplements in patients with sepsis and other critical conditions.", "CRITICAL PATIENT:A critical patient is an individual who is in a life-threatening condition that necessitates intensive medical care and monitoring. These patients often require specialized nutritional support as part of their treatment. The care provided to critical patients is crucial due to the severity of their health status, highlighting the need for comprehensive medical attention.", "GLN:Glutamine (Gln) is another amino acid discussed in the context of nutritional support for critically ill patients, but its supplementation is not recommended due to lack of demonstrated benefits.", "FIBER ENRICHED FORMULAS:Fiber enriched formulas are nutritional preparations that include fiber to aid in digestion and nutrient absorption, but their routine use is not recommended in critical patients."], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small", "temperature": 0.0, "frequency_penalty": null, "presence_penalty": null, "top_p": 1.0, "max_tokens": 4000, "n": 1}, "history": null}